; The same claim as 340, written one line HIGHER.
;
; An AXTAG attaches to the declaration that FOLLOWS it, so a tag above
; the `::` belongs to the SIGNATURE and a tag between `::` and `fn`
; belongs to the function. `checkAxtags` only ever runs on a `fn`, so
; until 2026-08-18 this placement was collected, carried, printed by
; `symbols` on the function's own line - and never checked. The two
; readers disagreed: `symbols` showed `#pure` and `#effects=IO` side by
; side while `check` answered OK.
;
; It is the more natural placement of the two, which is why it went
; unnoticed: an annotation above a whole declaration reads as being
; about the whole declaration.
;
; The span is the FUNCTION's name, not the tag's line, because the
; claim is about the function and `emitAxtag` has always anchored there.
;@axiom:pure
(:: emit (-> Int Int))

(fn (emit fd)
  {
    (__syscall3 1 fd 0 0)
    (alloc Int 1)
  }
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
